{title: Seven Ewe Lambs}
{subtitle: Genesis 21:22–34}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Abimelech came with Pikol
Said God is with [Bb]you in all
[C]Swear to me by [Gm]the Lord
[Am]Do not deal false[Dm]ly at all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Seven ewe lambs [C]set [Bb]apart
Witness [C]to the [Dm]well you dug
Beersheba the oath [C]was sworn
[Bb]The cove[Am]nant made [Dm]by trust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You took my well by [C]force
[Bb]I did not know who [C]did it
[Dm]Now I see your [C]anger rise
[Bb]I have heard [Am]nothing of it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Seven little lambs set a[C]part
[Bb]Witness to the [C]well you [Dm]dug
Beersheba the oath was [C]sworn
The [Bb]covenant [Am]made by [Dm]trust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Sheep and cattle were [C]given
The [Bb]two made a co[C]venant
[Dm]Pikol left to his [C]land
[Bb]Abraham [Am]stayed in the [Dm]dust
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
He [Bb]planted a tamarisk [C]tree
[Dm]Called on the name of the [C]Lord
The [Bb]Everlasting God [C]heard
[Bb]His prayer [Am]in the [Dm]desert
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Seven ewe lambs as [C]witness
The [Bb]well dug in the [Dm]sand
The name of the Lord re[C]membered
In the [Bb]land of the Philis[Dm]tines
{end_of_verse}
